I thank authors for the rebuttal.

Authors confirm that
 - their approach is far behind state-of-the-art in a well-know click-based instance segmentation task;
 - they are not the first to train instance segmentation on top of pre-trained generative model;
 - there exist even training-free approaches to do it.

Based on this, I don't see reasonable novelty, and keep my original score.
